<section class="bio">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <figure class="portrait"><img src="/assets/jas-portrait.jpg" alt="Portrait of José Ángel Sosa López" loading="lazy"></figure>
      <h2>Background</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="copy">
      <p>My work started in industrial design — physical objects, materials, production constraints — before moving into retail POS and EPOS product management, and from there into IT program and portfolio leadership across financial services, banking, retail, SaaS and consumer goods.</p>
      <p>That origin shapes how I approach digital products and technology portfolios today: as things with materials, tolerances and maintenance costs, whether they're built from plastic or from code. I call this way of working DTL — Digital Transformation Leadership — and it operates at program and portfolio scale, across distributed, cross-functional teams.</p>
      <p><em>Thinking in Products, Building Systems</em>, the living book on this site, is where I write that argument out in full, one chapter a week.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

