<section class="principles">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <ul class="plist">
      <li><b>Materials before roadmaps</b><span>Naming real constraints — cost, latency, headcount — before committing to a plan.</span></li>
      <li><b>Product and project, not product versus project</b><span>Portfolio leadership works when both disciplines share the same evidence.</span></li>
      <li><b>Evidence over narrative</b><span>Case work and shipped systems, not slide decks, are what should carry an argument.</span></li>
      <li><b>Governance without bureaucracy</b><span>Enough process to make good decisions repeatable — no more than that.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

